              "alt": "Schematic in two rows. The brain: experience, then the hippocampus (fast; keeps episodes apart), then replay in sleep and quiet rest into the neocortex (slow; connections change). Claude with agent memory: session, then the transcript (word for word, kept), then dreaming between tasks into notes and wiki (read back as input). Under the notes, hatched, the model weights, unchanged; no arrow reaches the model",
              "caption": "Fig. 1 — Two ways to keep what happened, as a schematic. In the brain, replay teaches the neocortex, so the system that remembers is itself changed. In Claude, dreaming writes notes that are read back as input in the next session; the model's weights stay as they were.",
